"Let $\\Sigma$ be a $(d-1)$-dimensional complex admitting a convex-ear decomposition, and let $S\\subseteq [d]$. Write $P_\\Sigma$ for the face poset of $\\Sigma$, and $(P_\\Sigma)_S$ for its rank-selected subposet; let $\\Delta((P_\\Sigma)_S)$ denote the order complex of this subposet. **Convex-ear decomposition inheritance claim.** The complex\n\n$$\n\\Delta((P_\\Sigma)_S)\n$$\n\nadmits a convex-ear decomposition. The claim gives a sufficient condition for rank-selected order complexes of face posets to retain convex-ear decompositions; the surrounding text notes that the analogous assertion can fail when $d\\in S$, so the precise range of the theorem and its hypotheses are important."